> All the world's a stage, and we are mere players.
> — Roccia
 She is a gifted improvisational comedian and the First Mate of the [[Troupe of Fools]]. While bashful and introverted, she, alongside '''Pero''', her closest companion, possesses a repertoire of tools and talents to protect and nurture her friends and newfound family.

==Official Introduction==
> Roccia is a gifted improvisational comedian and the First Mate of the Fool's Troupe, known for her mastery of stage props.
With a tranquil, composed disposition, she navigates the ship's quarters, perched atop her giant box, meticulously ensuring the Troupe remains orderly and tidy.
> — [https://wutheringwaves.kurogames.com/en/main#resonators Introduction from the Official Website.]

==Trivia==
* Roccia's Convene quote "All the world's a stage, and we are mere players" is a reference to a line from Shakespeare's ''As You Like It'', "All the world’s a stage, And all the men and women merely players."
* The name Roccia is a word of Italian origin and means "Rock".